module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_frozen_population_hides_a_compile_refusal

// WHY THIS ROW IS ENROLLED HERE AND NOT ONLY IN THE DROP PR. The two rows named below sat in the
// frozen population of `gunbc.witness.witness_deferral_freeze` while both were red. stern-bat-401's
// rule for that drop is that no red sits inside it, so each red must either leave the frozen list
// or carry this kind of row with a named owner. Neither leaves: both causes are real and unowned
// until the owner below lands their change. So this row is the owner-carrying alternative, written
// where the drop's claim can see it.

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_frozen_population_hides_a_compile_refusal: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_frozen_population_hides_a_compile_refusal" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**an entry kept out of the executing lanes by a freeze hides that the entry's own tree references a declaration nothing can resolve.** A deferral freeze stops the claim; the freeze is also, in practice, why nobody reads the claim's refusal. The refusal is not lost by the freeze -- it is lost by nobody looking, because the lane that would have looked is exactly the lane the freeze withdrew.",

    "TWO ENTRIES, TWO STACKED LAYERS, BOTH AT MAIN (read at origin/main d6586c4e450a, triaged for the drop in gunbc#14886). `enforcement_consistency_gate_holds` (src/v2/test/claim/enforcement_live_witness.dag) fails for two causes stacked, and the second is behind the first: (A) src/v2/lens/enforcement/inventory.dag:272:17 calls `witness_consumer_cadence_for_row` and `witness_row_excluded_from_discovery` from `v2.workflow.witness_admission` with NO import of them -- the refusal is 'cannot establish the declaration identity ... no declaration is indexed'; and (B) BEHIND IT, `lens_contract_schedule_lens` (src/v2/lens/enforcement/contract.dag:434) binds `BoundConsumerWitness { file: 'src/v2/test/claim/walk_plan_schedule_lens_test.dag', function: 'gunbc_ci_walk_plan_schedule_lens_holds' }` to a file that no longer exists. `git log --all --diff-filter=D -- <that path>` names the remover: 611fd0277082, 'FLOOR-Y cutover: delete the CI floor, rebuild from the run_required_floor seed' (gunbc#8283, merged 2026-08-17). The binding was never re-pointed in the ~9 weeks since. A #14887-only tree -- which fixes (A) -- STILL fails the gate, which is how (B) is known to be real and not speculative (keen-owl-704's control; this row's read of the binding and the removal is independent and agrees).",

    "`cost_coverage_smoke_totality_holds` (src/v2/test/claim/enforcement/cost_coverage_witness.dag) fails at src/v2/lens/enforcement/cost_coverage.dag:89:9 and :97:17 for the same KIND of cause as (A) and with no second layer: `judge_subject_node` and `asymptotic_class_of_cost` are used with no import of their declaring modules (receipts.dag:44 and cost.dag:965 -- both functions are LIVE on main, so this is not a rename and the index is not stale about them). gunbai-bot's gunbc#14887 declares the imports and its own PR body carries a head-built PASS receipt for this claim at 0c7db6dfe9da, so this entry's cause is read and named, not guessed.",

    "WHY NO GATE CAUGHT IT: the three functions exist, so no removal check fires; nothing compiles these entries outside the frozen lane, so nothing reaches the import error; and the schedule-lens binding is a STRING inside a typed carrier, which DESIGN §3 already names a second representation that cannot be checked by holding the type. The refusal is loud for whoever dispatches the entry. Nobody dispatches a frozen entry.",

    "NAMED OWNERS (route each to its owner, as required of every row here): layer (A) plus the whole cost_coverage entry are owned by **gunbai-bot** in open gunbc#14887 (add the imports); its own PR body carries a head-built PASS receipt for `cost_coverage_smoke_totality_holds` at 0c7db6dfe9da. Layer (B)'s disposition is RETIREMENT, ruled by **warm-wolf-570**: the schedule lens judged a CI-floor WalkPlan that #8283 deleted and has no production caller -- its only caller was its own synthetic witness. **keen-owl-704** carries the retirement on branch c4-enforcement-consistency (head e622ce43533a, PR number to follow): it deletes the contract binding, the lens_registry_v0 row, the ScheduleLens id, `v2.lens.schedule_lens`, the witness, and the witness's enrolment. When #14887 and the retirement PR both land and both entries pass, THIS row is where their receipts are recorded and the two freeze entries leave the population.",

    "HOW THIS IS DIFFERENT FROM THE NEIGHBOURING ROWS. `a_bare_type_name_binds_the_wrong_declaration` (gunbc#12494) is the same population gap for one bare name inside one entry; this row is the same shape reached through a *typed* carrier's string field, which the import fix does not touch. `bare_name_resolved_only_by_the_flat_namespace` covers a name that resolves whole-tree and refuses entry-alone; here the name resolves in NEITHER, and the only reason main is green is that the lane is frozen. `symbol_index_edge_introduces_no_declarations` (#14055, routed to stern-bat-401 for an owner) is the producer side -- an index that misses live declarations; this row's index read is the opposite (the declaration is live and the index knows it; the file itself is absent) so it is not that defect, and is cited here so a later reader does not file it twice.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.enforcement.inventory", decl_name: "cadence_scheduling_rows_for_witness", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.enforcement.contract", decl_name: "lens_contract_schedule_lens", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.lens.enforcement.cost_coverage", decl_name: "cost_coverage_fn_verdict_from_body", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.enforcement_live_witness", decl_name: "enforcement_consistency_gate_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.enforcement.cost_coverage_witness", decl_name: "cost_coverage_smoke_totality_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.witness.witness_deferral_freeze", decl_name: "frozen_path_deferrals", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
